------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  xttestpanel -- full panel diagnostic report
  dependent variable: y   model: fe
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Heteroskedasticity test  --  one-way fixed effects (within residuals)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
H0: homoskedastic idiosyncratic disturbances
Auxiliary regressors (z):  x1 x2 x3 x4
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test                                              stat    df    p-val
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Breusch-Pagan / Holly-Gardiol LM               25.2191     4   0.0000 ***
Koenker (studentized, robust) LM               23.4542     4   0.0001 ***
Juhl-Sosa-Escudero F (FE within)                5.9743     4   0.0001 ***
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* p<.10 ** p<.05 *** p<.01.  Refs: Juhl & Sosa-Escudero (2014); Feng et al.
(2020).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Serial-correlation tests  --  fixed effects (within) residuals
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
H0: no first-order (AR/MA) serial correlation in the idiosyncratic errors
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test                                              stat    df    p-val
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Baltagi-Li LM (AR(1)/MA(1), 2-sided)           46.6014     1   0.0000 ***
Born-Breitung / Wooldridge                     18.0135     1   0.0000 ***
Bin Chen (2022) robust portmanteau             18.0135     1   0.0000 ***
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
rho_hat (lag-1 residual autocorr.) = 0.2095.  * p<.10 ** p<.05 *** p<.01.
Refs: Baltagi & Li (1995); Baltagi, Jung & Song (2010); Chen (2022).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Cross-sectional dependence tests  --  fixed effects (within) residuals
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
H0: cross-sectional independence (errors uncorrelated across units)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test                                              stat    df    p-val
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pesaran (2004) CD                              54.1064     .   0.0000 ***
Baltagi-Kao-Peng (2016) bias-corr. CD          43.7399     .   0.0000 ***
Breusch-Pagan (1980) LM                      4502.9857  1225   0.0000 ***
Pesaran scaled LM (LM_adj)                     66.2253     .   0.0000 ***
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mean|rho_ij| = 0.3716, mean rho_ij = 0.3457.
Refs: Pesaran (2004,2015); Baltagi, Kao & Peng (2016); Breusch & Pagan (1980).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Multicollinearity diagnostics  --  fe (within) design
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Variable                          VIF    robust VIF         tol
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
x1                              1.137         1.126      0.8792
x2                            103.018        99.844      0.0097
x3                            102.880        99.757      0.0097
x4                              1.005         1.004      0.9954
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Mean VIF = 52.010, mean robust VIF = 50.433.
Rule of thumb: VIF>10 (tol<0.1) signals serious collinearity. Robust VIF (RVIF,
WGM-FIMGT) is resistant to high-leverage collinearity-enhancing obs.
Ref: Ismaeel, Midi & Sani (2021).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Specification test: fixed vs random effects
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
H0: random effects estimator is consistent (cov(x, mu_i)=0)
classical = Stata's Hausman contrast; robust = Huber-weighted Mundlak test
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test                                              stat    df    p-val
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Hausman chi2 (classical)                      144.2013     4   0.0000 ***
Robust weighted Hausman (Beyaztas)            134.0867     4   0.0000 ***
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Downweighted share of obs. = 16.5% (Huber tuning c=1.345).  Large gap between
the two => influential/outlying obs.
Decision rule: reject H0 => prefer FE.  Refs: Mundlak (1978); Beyaztas et al.
(2021).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Functional-form test (Lin, Li & Sun 2014)  --  fixed effects
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
H0: the parametric (linear) functional form is correctly specified
Ha: a nonparametric alternative fits better
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test                                              stat      p-val
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Lin-Li-Sun J_n (standardized)                  10.7997     0.0000  (asymptotic N(
> 0,1))
  wild-bootstrap p-value (B=99)                            0.0100
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
bandwidth = 0.4217 (Silverman rule x scale).  Ref: Lin, Li & Sun (2014).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  SUMMARY -- decisions at 5% level
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Heteroskedasticity (BP/Koenker)           p=0.0001  REJECT H0
Serial correlation (Baltagi-Li)           p=0.0000  REJECT H0
Serial correlation (Chen 2022)            p=0.0000  REJECT H0
Cross-section dep. (Pesaran CD)           p=0.0000  REJECT H0
Cross-section dep. (BKP 2016)             p=0.0000  REJECT H0
Functional form (Lin-Li-Sun)              p=0.0100  REJECT H0
FE vs RE (Hausman)                        p=0.0000  REJECT H0
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Mean VIF = 52.010 (collinearity if >10).
